card.statement:
(a)
All matrices in a sufficiently small neighborhood of

\begin{equation*}
J_m(\lambda)\oplus
J_n(\lambda),\qquad m\le n
\end{equation*}

are similar to matrices
of the form

\begin{equation}
J_{m-r}(\lambda)
\oplus J_{n+r}(\lambda),\qquad 0\le r\le m.
\end{equation}

(b) Each matrix <<ref:cfq>> with $r>0$ is similar to

\begin{equation}
\mat{J_m(\lambda )&\Delta_r(\varepsilon )^T\\0&J_n(\lambda )},
\end{equation}

in which $\Delta_r(\varepsilon )$ is defined in <<ref:rdpd>>, and $\varepsilon$ is an arbitrary nonzero complex number.
